shura.cpp: sources and licenses

shura.cpp is released under the MIT License. It combines code from these sources, all under the MIT License:

1. llama.cpp (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp)
   Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors. The upstream LICENSE and AUTHORS files are kept unchanged. The `upstream` branch is
   ggml-org/llama.cpp master; the `shura` branch is rebased on it (currently upstream commit 74bca3950).

2. thecodacus/llama.cpp, branch `perf` (https://github.com/thecodacus/llama.cpp), by Anirban Kar
   The starting point of this fork: a snapshot taken on 2026-09-03 (upstream commit 42f0225fe at the time). From it come the
   MoE expert cache in VRAM (hot expert packs, static placement), the scheduler's expert prefetch and CPU worker, pinning of the
   CPU experts, tools/moe-trace and the qwen4exp conversion support.

3. TheTom/llama-cpp-turboquant, branch `feature/turboquant-kv-cache` (https://github.com/TheTom/llama-cpp-turboquant)
   The TurboQuant KV cache types (after arXiv 2504.19874), their CUDA and HIP flash-attention kernels and the rotation data,
   which came into the snapshot in (2).

4. Changes written for Shura, Copyright (c) 2026 hikkian
   The VRAM governor and its endpoints, pause with a checkpoint and resume, live resize of the expert cache with a
   rollback-safe release, the bounded LRU, hybrid and two-channel cache policies, the loader options (direct I/O, page-cache
   drop, pinned memory limit), the CUDA/HIP kernels and fixes listed in docs/SHURA.md, and the tests for them.

The parts from (2) and (3) were moved onto a current upstream as commits of this branch, so the git history of this repository
does not show their authors; this file, README.md and docs/SHURA.md do. Model weights are not part of this repository and are
covered by their own licenses.
